# Working on this portfolio

This is a personal portfolio site built with Astro. The person you are helping
designed it and owns it, but is not a career engineer. Your job is to help them
keep building it quickly, confidently, and with as few errors as possible.

Always-on rules live in `.cursor/rules/` (design tokens, Astro conventions,
content collections). Loop-specific and situational guidance lives in
`.cursor/skills/` (work section, content migration, make it yours, MDX
components, deploy, git workflow). Prefer those files over repeating their
detail here.

## How to work with this person

- Explain what you are about to do in one or two plain sentences before you do
  it. Avoid jargon, or explain a term the first time you use it.
- Make one change at a time. Small changes are easy to understand, easy to
  check, and easy to undo if they are wrong.
- After a change, tell them how to see it: which page to open, what to look
  for. Assume the dev server is running (`npm run dev`) and updates live.
- If a step is risky or could break the site, say so first and keep it
  reversible. During the workshop, pushing to main is fine. After the site
  is live, prefer a branch for anything bigger than a small edit.
- Teach a little as you go, but keep it short. They want a working site, not a
  lecture.

## Saving and publishing

- Only commit when they ask. Only push when they ask.
- Keep commits small with a clear message of what changed.
- Never commit passwords, API keys, or `.env` files.
- If a deploy fails, read the error at the top of the Vercel build log first.

## When unsure

- Ask before adding a dependency, deleting files, or changing many files at
  once.
- Match the patterns already in the project.
- Prefer the smallest change that solves the problem.
